#   cold = hash self + copy + fsync + verify (a version's first spawn in a home): p50 177-192 ms, p99 211-221 ms
#   warm = hash self + verify the existing copy (every later spawn):              p50 29-35 ms,   p99 31-40 ms
#   (An earlier -count=3 run under heavier co-load: cold p50 189-200 / p99 249-353 ms, warm p50 38-44 / p99 44-49 ms.)
#
# (2) End to end, the real binary: a cold 'qompack session-start' (no daemon running) per fresh project,
# 10 runs per mode: bash plans/sdd/V6-closeout/w2-lifetime/runs/34-c117-stage-cost.sh <repo> <scratch> 10
# (unstaged = bare binary, no plugin layout, the pre-C1.17 path; staged-cold = plugin layout +
# CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT, fresh home each run; staged-warm = one home already holding the copy).
#   unstaged     n=10 min=443 p50=570  max=2419 ms
#   staged-cold  n=10 min=891 p50=1540 max=3053 ms
#   staged-warm  n=10 min=381 p50=466  max=706 ms
# No run spooled its own session.start: in every mode the daemon was reachable before EnsureRunning's
# 1.5 s poll ended. Every staged daemon ran from <home>\.qompack\bin\<sha256>\qompack.exe; every
# unstaged one from the bare binary. The script stopped each daemon by the pid in its own lock file.
#
# Reading: the copy itself is ~0.2 s; most of staged-cold's extra ~1 s is the first execution of a
# just-written executable (the unstaged mode's first two runs, of a just-built binary, show the same
# 1.8-2.4 s). That happens once per version per user; warm spawns cost no more than unstaged ones.
# Budget fit: staging runs in session-start's preSend (EnsureRunning), before the client dials, so it is
# outside both the client's 10 s reply deadline (which starts at awaitReply) and the route's 5 s compact
# budget (which starts at the request's arrival). What bounds it is the host's 15 s SessionStart
# timeout: process start + stageBinary (cold p99 ~0.35 s) + EnsureRunning's 1.5 s poll (which caps a
# slow first execution: past it Send spools and the compact client writes the deferred note) + the 10 s
# reply deadline leaves >2.5 s of margin. No change made; staging ahead of time would only move the
# same one-off cost.
#
